{"code":"47-2221.00","title":"Structural Iron and Steel Workers","description":"Raise, place, and unite iron or steel girders, columns, and other structural members to form completed structures or structural frameworks. May erect metal storage tanks and assemble prefabricated metal buildings.","jobZone":2,"kinds":{"R":{"score":7,"share":0.5291},"I":{"score":2.79,"share":0.1578},"A":{"score":1.41,"share":0.0362},"S":{"score":1.17,"share":0.015},"E":{"score":1.24,"share":0.0212},"C":{"score":3.73,"share":0.2407}},"highPoints":["R","C"],"tasks":[{"id":11544,"text":"Read specifications or blueprints to determine the locations, quantities, or sizes of materials required.","core":true,"importance":4.47,"relevance":94.83,"frequency":5.64},{"id":11545,"text":"Verify vertical and horizontal alignment of structural steel members, using plumb bobs, laser equipment, transits, or levels.","core":true,"importance":4.07,"relevance":93.21,"frequency":4.48},{"id":11556,"text":"Erect metal or precast concrete components for structures, such as buildings, bridges, dams, towers, storage tanks, fences, or highway guard rails.","core":true,"importance":4.06,"relevance":93.24,"frequency":4.77},{"id":11548,"text":"Bolt aligned structural steel members in position for permanent riveting, bolting, or welding into place.","core":true,"importance":4.04,"relevance":100,"frequency":4.82},{"id":24053,"text":"Assemble or inspect hoisting equipment or rigging, such as cables, pulleys, or hooks, to move heavy equipment or materials.","core":true,"importance":4.04,"relevance":91.81,"frequency":4.61},{"id":11550,"text":"Fabricate metal parts, such as steel frames, columns, beams, or girders, according to blueprints or instructions from supervisors.","core":true,"importance":4.02,"relevance":78.42,"frequency":null},{"id":24054,"text":"Lift steel beams, girders, or columns using cranes or forklifts, or by signaling hoisting equipment operators to lift or position structural steel members.","core":true,"